  "data": {
    "ruleType": "army-rule",
    "summary": "As your Command phase begins, you may choose a Combat Doctrine for your friendly ADEPTUS ASTARTES units. It lasts until your next Command phase begins. Assault Doctrine lets a unit declare a charge after an advance move that turn. Devastator Doctrine gives its ranged attacks [ASSAULT]. Tactical Doctrine permits shooting and declaring charges that turn, even after a fall-back move. Each unit may use a given doctrine only once each battle unless another rule provides an exception. If a fresh doctrine takes effect for a unit, its previous doctrine ends.",
